# Directories and files that must not enter the knowledge graph.
#
# The rule: index what a reader of this repository would read. Virtual
# environments, build output, dependency trees and generated caches are
# noise - they are large, they change on every install, and they contain
# no decisions worth recording.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Version control and tool state
.git/
.graphify/
*.log

# Generated and runtime data
artifacts/
storage/
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# The application's own artifact root, and the copy the test suite writes
# into. Both live under the repository root because a relative artifact
# path is resolved against REPO_ROOT, so `var/artifacts` holds real scans
# and `var/test-artifacts` holds the last test run's scans. Neither is
# source, and both are large and rewritten constantly: left in, they were
# 45% of the graph and described the project's own test runs instead of
# the project.
var/

# Graphify's own incremental cache (the graph itself is committed)
graphify-out/cache/

# Lockfiles and minified output
package-lock.json
*.lock
*.min.js
